From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:05:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Say what clearing the memory costs
 here

The help of "Clear memory at power-on" says about 1 s with 32 GB, the
figure of the W541. On an M920x with 40 GB, the BS_DEV_INIT exit hook
that clears it takes 2003 ms of a boot (cbmem -1), about 0.5 s for
each 10 GB, the most expensive step after the serial console.

TEST=cbmem -1 on an M920x with 32 + 8 GB: "BS: BS_DEV_INIT exit times
(exec / console): 2003 / 110 ms", the clear_memory lines inside it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
index 6ae81352d1..4df7e0b67b 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cfr.c
@@ -473,7 +473,8 @@ static const struct sm_object clear_dram_on_boot = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.ui_name	= "Clear memory at power-on",
 	.ui_helptext	= "Clear all the memory at every boot (not when resuming\n"
 			  "from sleep), so that what the previous OS left in it\n"
-			  "cannot be read. About 1 s more per boot with 32 GB.\n"
+			  "cannot be read. About 0.5 s more per boot for each 10 GB:\n"
+			  "2 s with 40 GB.\n"
 			  "Default: on.",
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
